The recent findings from the Belle II and LHCb experiments, specifically the anomalies in $b 	o c$ transitions, have been examined in the context of the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay within the $U_1$ leptoquark framework. The $U_1$ leptoquark model, which involves a scalar leptoquark with electric charge $5/3$, has been applied to the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay. Theoretical predictions for the branching ratio and form factor of this decay have been calculated, and the results indicate that the $U_1$ leptoquark model can provide a suitable explanation for the observed branching ratio of the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay. Furthermore, the $U_1$ leptoquark model can be tested through the measurement of the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay's form factor, which can be determined by analyzing the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay spectrum.
